---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';

const host = new URL(SITE.url).host;
---

<Base title={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE.name}`} description={`How ${host} handles your data: what you type into the calculators stays in your browser and is never sent to us.`}>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">Last updated {SITE.policyUpdated}.</p>

    <section>
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        What you type into the calculators on {host} stays in your browser. It is not sent to us, and we have no accounts, no advertising and no
        tracking cookies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What the calculators store</h2>
      <p>
        The time card calculator saves the card you are working on, and any cards you choose to save by name, in your browser's local storage on your
        own device. This is what lets a card still be there when you come back. We cannot see it, and it is not copied anywhere else.
      </p>
      <p>
        To remove it, use Clear or Delete on the time card, or clear this site's data in your browser settings. Using a private or incognito window
        means nothing is kept after you close it.
      </p>
      <p>The other calculators and converters do not store anything.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Share links</h2>
      <p>
        "Copy share link" puts the contents of the time card into the link itself, in the part after the # sign. Browsers do not send that part of an
        address to any server, so we never receive it. Anyone you give the link to can read the card, including the name and hourly rate on it, so share
        it only with people who should see it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What our hosting provider receives</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted by Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare receives the technical details of each request, such as your IP address, the
        page requested, and your browser type, in order to deliver the page and protect the site from abuse. Cloudflare handles this information under
        its own <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Cookies, analytics and third parties</h2>
      <p>
        We do not set cookies. We do not run analytics, advertising or social media scripts, and the pages load no fonts or code from other companies.
        We do not sell or share personal information, because we do not collect any.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some pages link to government websites as sources for overtime rules. Those sites have their own privacy policies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        If you email us, we receive your address and whatever you write, and use them only to reply.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we add analytics, advertising or anything else that changes what is collected, we will update this page and the date at the top before it
        takes effect.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
